{# ── ONE MESSAGE OF SUPPORT, RENDERED ONCE ────────────────────────────────────
   Used by the wall on the ballot AND by /vote/{prog}/{slug}/messages. One renderer,
   so a change to how somebody's words are displayed — or to what the report button
   does — cannot land in one place and not the other.

   Context: m (a row from VoteMessageService::wall).

   `m.name` has ALREADY been resolved against the voter's consent by the service and
   arrives as "A supporter" where consent was not given. Nothing here has the real
   name in scope, which is deliberate: a template that held it would be one edit away
   from printing it. #}
<li class="vmi" x-data="vmItem('{{ m.token|e('js') }}', {{ m.cheers|default(0) }})">
  <p class="vmi__b">{{ m.body }}</p>
  <footer class="vmi__f">
    <span class="vmi__n">{{ m.name }}</span>
    {% if m.source == 'paid' %}<span class="vmi__tag">backed with votes</span>{% endif %}

    <button type="button" class="vmi__act" :class="mine && 'is-on'" @click="cheer()" :disabled="busy"
            :aria-label="mine ? 'You cheered this' : 'Cheer this message'">
      <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3ZM7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3"/></svg>
      <span x-text="n > 0 ? n : 'Cheer'">{{ m.cheers ?: 'Cheer' }}</span>
    </button>

    {% if m.token %}
    <a class="vmi__act" href="/m/{{ m.token }}">Share this</a>
    {# ── THE REPORT BUTTON ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Quiet, last, and open to anybody — including a stranger who arrived from a
       WhatsApp link. These messages are about named people, many of them children,
       so the person best placed to notice something wrong is a reader who knows
       them and who is never going to register an account to say so.

       One tap, no form: a reason field would be another screen between seeing
       something and reporting it, and the moderator is going to read the message
       either way. The reply is the same whether this is the first report or the one
       that trips the threshold. #}
    <button type="button" class="vmi__act vmi__act--report" @click="report()" x-show="!reported" x-cloak
            aria-label="Report this message">Report</button>
    <span class="vmi__done" x-show="reported" x-cloak>Reported ✓</span>
    {% endif %}
  </footer>
</li>
